{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Blink bundle feels like a useful next step after my Blink XT2 camera because a doorbell and additional cameras could extend coverage around my home.",
    "The Echo interests me because Alexa voice control could make my Fire TV and compatible security devices more convenient to use together."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The earbuds and portable speaker do not serve the home viewing and security needs reflected in my recent purchases, and I am not currently looking for personal or portable audio.",
    "Another HD Fire TV Stick feels redundant after my 4K stick and Fire TV television, while the Samsung remote has no clear compatibility with my Toshiba TV.",
    "Ethernet cables and a 16TB drive could have uses, but my purchases do not establish a current need for five cables or that much storage."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying electronics seems to have been treated as a reason to recommend other electronics, even when they serve very different purposes.",
    "My Fire TV purchases seem to have been taken as interest in another streaming stick, without considering what a new device would add to what I already own."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I am more interested in additions that extend my existing home setup, such as broader camera coverage or convenient voice control.",
    "Compatibility with my specific devices matters: a TV accessory needs to work with my Toshiba, and a security addition needs to fit my existing setup.",
    "I need a concrete reason to buy an accessory; a possible connection to my equipment alone is not enough."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my connected-home interests but miss the distinction between useful additions, redundant devices, and unrelated electronics."
}"}
